            <ArticleTitle>Measurement of Kinetic Isotope Effects in an Enzyme-Catalyzed Reaction by Continuous-Flow Mass Spectrometry.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>149-161</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0076-6879(17)30231-8</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/bs.mie.2017.07.001</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Kinetic isotope effects (KIEs) provide powerful probes of the mechanisms of enzyme-catalyzed reactions. In this chapter, we describe the use of continuous-flow mass spectrometry to determine the deuterium KIE for the enzyme N-acetylpolyamine oxidase based on the ratio of labeled and unlabeled products in mass spectra of whole reaction mixtures.</AbstractText>
